Widen skolems in retains sets to the top capability

An inline expansion that substitutes an unstable argument into a
dependent result's capture set (e.g. a given of type
`(tactic: Tactic) => (X is Decodable)^{tactic, caps.any}` applied
during summonInline with a non-path tactic) leaves a SkolemType in the
@retains annotation of the inliner's evidence proxy val. The proxy's
type is explicit, so Setup interprets the annotation as written and
toCapability rejected the skolem with "Illegal capture reference:
(?1 : Any)" — an error the user can neither cause nor avoid in source,
and one that comes and goes with symbol-completion order (zinc and
batch compilation gave opposite verdicts on the same file). Skolem
infos are already erased to Any by RetainingAnnotation.sanitize, so
the underlying captures cannot be recovered; widen the skolem to
caps.any, the standard sound over-approximation for a capability that
cannot be named.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Enabled by `-Z:retains-skolems`; without it, upstream's code runs at every site this
patch touches.

